{% doc %}
  @prompt
    Create a custom Shopify FAQ section with a modern, premium layout.
    
    SECTION STRUCTURE
    - Two-column layout on desktop:
      - Left side: FAQ items (50% width)
      - Right side: FAQ items (50% width)
    - Split the FAQs evenly between left and right columns
    - On mobile: stack into a single column (left first, then right)
    - Use accordion-style FAQs (click to expand/collapse)
    
    FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS
    - Disable any theme slider, carousel, or auto-rotation for this section
    - FAQs must open/close smoothly with animation
    - Only one FAQ open at a time per column (optional but preferred)
    - Lightweight hover effects on FAQ cards (subtle lift or glow)
    
    CONTENT (USE EXACT TEXT)
    LEFT COLUMN FAQs:
    Q: What is Entitled?
    A: A members-only storefront for curated, limited-quantity clothing — top-tier quality, always.
    
    Q: Is membership paid?
    A: No. Membership is free and granted through approval.
    
    Q: How do I become a member?
    A: Apply with your details. Approval is typically granted within 10–15 days.
    
    Q: Can I shop without membership?
    A: No. If you are not a member, you cannot access the store.
    
    Q: Who is a customer?
    A: Only members. If you are not a member, you are not a customer.
    
    Q: What details do you collect for membership?
    A: Name, mobile number, email address, and shipping address.
    
    RIGHT COLUMN FAQs:
    Q: What do members get?
    A: Membership is the customer identity. It grants store access and members-first support.
    
    Q: How is access priced?
    A: Pricing reflects member access, verification, and availability.
    
    Q: Are the products authentic?
    A: Yes. We handpick from select authentic channels and verify quality before listing.
    
    Q: Do you sell factory rejects or quality rejects?
    A: No. Items that fail our quality standard are not listed.
    
    Q: Are drops restocked?
    A: By default, no. Drops open and close. When they close, they become archive.
    
    Q: What is your return policy?
    A: No-questions-asked returns, subject to basic condition verification and fair use. Approved returns are issued as store credits only.
    
    Q: Do you have purchase limits?
    A: No purchase limits at this time. Limits may be introduced later if needed.
    
    Q: How can I contact support?
    A: WhatsApp customer support (details on the website). Members-first resolution.
    
    DESIGN & STYLE
    - Background:
      - Plain gradient grey color palette
      - Example: soft light grey → dark grey gradient
      - Add very subtle texture overlay if possible
      - Optional faint T-shirt doodle or fabric-style texture in the background (low opacity, non-distracting)
    - FAQ Cards:
      - Slightly darker/lighter than background for contrast
      - Rounded corners
      - Soft shadow
    - Typography:
      - Bold questions
      - Clean, readable answers
    - Hover Effect:
      - Smooth transition
      - Slight upward movement or glow
    - Animation:
      - Accordion open/close animation (ease-in-out)
      - Hover transitions under 300ms
    
    GENERAL NOTES
    - Keep the section premium, minimal, and modern
    - No flashy colors
    - No sliders
    - No autoplay
    - Focus on clarity and exclusivity
{% enddoc %}
{% assign ai_gen_id = block.id | replace: '_', '' | downcase %}

{% style %}
  .ai-faq-section-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, {{ block.settings.gradient_start }} 0%, {{ block.settings.gradient_end }} 100%);
    padding: {{ block.settings.section_padding }}px 20px;
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .ai-faq-section-{{ ai_gen_id }}::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    background-image: url('data:image/svg+xml;utf8,<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="100" height="100" viewBox="0 0 100 100"><rect x="0" y="0" width="1" height="1" fill="rgba(0,0,0,0.02)"/></svg>');
    background-size: 4px 4px;
    opacity: {{ block.settings.texture_opacity }};
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .ai-faq-container-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    max-width: {{ block.settings.max_width }}px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
  }

  .ai-faq-title-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    text-align: center;
    font-size: {{ block.settings.title_size }}px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: {{ block.settings.title_color }};
    margin: 0 0 {{ block.settings.title_spacing }}px;
    letter-spacing: 0.5px;
  }

  .ai-faq-subtitle-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    text-align: center;
    font-size: {{ block.settings.subtitle_size }}px;
    color: {{ block.settings.subtitle_color }};
    margin: 0 0 {{ block.settings.content_spacing }}px;
    opacity: 0.9;
  }

  .ai-faq-grid-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: {{ block.settings.column_gap }}px;
  }

  .ai-faq-column-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: {{ block.settings.item_gap }}px;
  }

  .ai-faq-item-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    background: {{ block.settings.card_background }};
    border-radius: {{ block.settings.card_radius }}px;
    box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, {{ block.settings.shadow_opacity }});
    overflow: hidden;
    transition: transform 0.25s ease, box-shadow 0.25s ease;
  }

  .ai-faq-item-{{ ai_gen_id }}:hover {
    transform: translateY(-{{ block.settings.hover_lift }}px);
    box-shadow: 0 {{ block.settings.hover_lift | times: 2 }}px {{ block.settings.hover_lift | times: 3 }}px rgba(0, 0, 0, {{ block.settings.shadow_opacity | times: 1.5 }});
  }

  .ai-faq-question-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    width: 100%;
    padding: {{ block.settings.question_padding }}px;
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
    text-align: left;
    cursor: pointer;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 15px;
    font-size: {{ block.settings.question_size }}px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: {{ block.settings.question_color }};
    transition: color 0.25s ease;
  }

  .ai-faq-question-{{ ai_gen_id }}:hover {
    color: {{ block.settings.question_hover_color }};
  }

  .ai-faq-icon-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 20px;
    height: 20px;
    transition: transform 0.3s ease;
  }

  .ai-faq-icon-{{ ai_gen_id }} svg {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    stroke: {{ block.settings.icon_color }};
  }

  .ai-faq-item-{{ ai_gen_id }}.active .ai-faq-icon-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    transform: rotate(180deg);
  }

  .ai-faq-answer-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    max-height: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    transition: max-height 0.3s ease-in-out, padding 0.3s ease-in-out;
  }

  .ai-faq-item-{{ ai_gen_id }}.active .ai-faq-answer-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    max-height: 500px;
    padding: 0 {{ block.settings.question_padding }}px {{ block.settings.question_padding }}px;
  }

  .ai-faq-answer-text-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    font-size: {{ block.settings.answer_size }}px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: {{ block.settings.answer_color }};
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 768px) {
    .ai-faq-grid-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .ai-faq-title-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      font-size: {{ block.settings.title_size | times: 0.8 }}px;
    }

    .ai-faq-subtitle-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      font-size: {{ block.settings.subtitle_size | times: 0.9 }}px;
    }

    .ai-faq-question-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      font-size: {{ block.settings.question_size | times: 0.9 }}px;
      padding: {{ block.settings.question_padding | times: 0.8 }}px;
    }

    .ai-faq-answer-text-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      font-size: {{ block.settings.answer_size | times: 0.9 }}px;
    }

    .ai-faq-item-{{ ai_gen_id }}.active .ai-faq-answer-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      padding: 0 {{ block.settings.question_padding | times: 0.8 }}px {{ block.settings.question_padding | times: 0.8 }}px;
    }
  }
{% endstyle %}

